From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eugene Feinberg <uge@persimmons.ai>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:42:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 35/37] [Moore] SimplifyRefs: lower reads of concat_ref and
 struct part-select refs

Two reference shapes reached MooreToCore and failed to legalize:

- moore.read of a moore.concat_ref: a compound assignment to a
  concatenation ({a, b} &= e) reads its left-hand side back. The read is
  now the concatenation of the reads; the assignment is already split.

- moore.dyn_extract_ref of a packed-struct reference: a dynamic part-select
  (s[i*W +: W]) is legal on any packed type, but LLHD has no bit-level
  projection of a struct signal. Reads become a dyn_extract of the
  struct's bit vector; blocking assignments become a read-modify-write of
  the whole struct through it (clear the range, or in the shifted value).

Non-blocking part-select assignments are deliberately left alone: a
read-modify-write would read the struct's current value, so of two
non-blocking part-selects in one block the second would undo the first.
They still fail to legalize, which a new test pins down.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
